Objective:To work with a Spring Core application using annotations, auto wiring, and bean configuration concepts.Concept Explanation: Inner beans are beans defined within the scope of another bean definition, typically used when a bean is used only within the context of its enclosing bean and doesn't need to be exposed to the rest of the application.  They help in managing the lifecycle and visibility of beans within the application context efficiently. Concept Implementation:The inner bean concept is implemented by defining the Loan bean within the scope of the Account bean's definition.  This encapsulates the Loan bean within the Account bean, ensuring it is used only within the context of the Account bean and doesn't need to be exposed to the rest of the application. The Loan bean is injected into the Account bean via constructor-based injection, ensuring that each Account object has its instance of the Loan object. Account-Loan InnerBeanAccount class with the below private attributes is provided as a part of code skeleton


 
  
